    "category": "datatype",
    "description": "Create a structure data type. Body fields must be a JSON array of objects; each object needs name and type, with optional offset. Example fields: [{\"name\":\"dwId\",\"type\":\"uint\",\"offset\":0},{\"name\":\"pNext\",\"type\":\"void *\",\"offset\":4}]. Type may be any resolvable Ghidra data type or existing struct name. Set replace_placeholder=true to delete a 1-byte demangler/placeholder type with the same name before creating. To change size of an existing struct in place, use resize_struct; for atomic delete+recreate, use recreate_struct (see docs/STRUCT_RESIZE_WORKFLOW.md).（上游 MCP headless 服务器）",
