    "category": "function",
    "description": "Set a parameter's or local's storage location to a register, register pair, or stack slot. Accepts 'EAX', 'EAX:4', 'R0:4,R2:4' or 'Stack[-0x10]:4'; size defaults to the variable's data-type length. Use this when the argument layout cannot be expressed by any calling convention. Setting a PARAMETER's storage switches the whole function to custom variable storage (reported as custom_storage_enabled). The storage is read back after the write and returned in 'storage'. On programs with multiple address spaces (e.g., embedded targets), prefix addresses with the space name (mem:1000) to avoid ambiguous resolution.（上游 MCP headless 服务器）",
